          )
        )
  )

;; sprite-menu's own state-51 override: real landing, issue 759, a2 rung's
;; own STEP 3. Not itself named on this rung's own plan (which cited
;; dropdown-item's own missing transition), but the actual gap behind it:
;; dropdown-item has no state-51 override anywhere in the donor (grep across
;; menu2.gc's own dead top level: zero hits for "method-set! dropdown-item
;; 51"), so it inherits whatever its nearest ancestor with a real override
;; held AT ITS OWN deftype time (menu2-h.gc), per Section E's own vtable-
;; snapshot class already responsible for the method-58/59/60 re-installs
;; elsewhere in this file. sprite-menu (dropdown-item's own ancestor through
;; prim-strip-menu/string-menu) is that nearest override in the donor
;; (menu2.gc's own gp-10 block; table row "(method-set! sprite-menu 51
;; gp-10)"), so the fix is landing sprite-menu's own real content here,
;; before the re-install below reads it.
;;
;; Fresh scoped redecode (this file's own header recipe). :event and :enter
;; (anon-functions 69/72) are decode-clean; :trans (anon-function 73, donor
;; label L605) carries one benign "failed type prop at 17" on the move-rate
;; read - self's own info-ptr trans-info is typed only the base
;; animation-info at that point, not the richer transition-info/dropdown-
;; trans-info subtype that actually carries enter-pos-x/running-pos-x/etc
;; (menu2-h.gc:479-494,1100-1103) - resolved by casting once at the point of
;; use. abs.s (the alpha-blend delta) is decompiler print-name notation, the
;; same class as this file's own header's sll/f2i list, with no real GOAL
;; equivalent of its own; resolved to a plain conditional negate. The two
;; joint-transform-plus-(-1792.0/-1840.0) constants in the else arm (enter-
;; anim not -1) match base-menu-init-by-other's own already-landed joint-
;; position computation byte for byte (menu2-installs.gc:848-861), so that
;; branch is transcribed against that precedent's own idiom rather than the
;; raw offsets.
;;
;; Confirmed load-bearing for this rung's own six dropdown rows:
;; lobby-menu-data.gc's own six dropdown-trans-info literals all set
;; enter-pos-x/y equal to running-pos-x/y (0.0/0.0), so the completion check
;; below (progress >= 1.0 OR enter-pos = running-pos) is already true on
;; this :trans's own first frame for every row - this is the actual
;; per-frame driver that moves each row out of state 51, not an event.
;; dropdown-item's own :code for this same slot, inherited from base-menu-
;; state-51 (real content, once the re-install below runs), only advances
;; past its own trailing (sleep-code) when 3d-menu-type is truthy
;; (menu2-installs.gc:1085-1097) - false for every dropdown row (widget
