;; base-menu slot 59 re-install: issue 759, a2 rung's own STEP 5, the a1
;; idiom (menu2-installs.gc:994-996) applied to the one slot this rung
;; fills. Section E's own vtable-snapshot hazard: menu2-h.o's deftype forms
;; run before base-menu's own real method-59 exists, so any subtype that
;; never gets its own method-59 override keeps the stale (nullptr) copy it
;; snapshotted at deftype time, and base-menu-init-by-other calls method 59
;; unconditionally on every spawned widget (menu2-installs.gc:871).
;;
;; jakx-logo-menu is the only type on this rung's own list (selection-
;; menu-manager, dropdown-item, jakx-logo-menu) that actually needs the
;; re-install: selection-menu-manager already carries its own real
;; base-menu-method-59 (menu2-installs.gc:605, landed by a1) and
;; dropdown-item now carries its own real base-menu-method-59 (landed
;; above, this same file) - both write their own vtable slot 59 directly
;; via their own defmethod's method-set!, so re-installing base-menu's
;; generic stub over either here would silently replace the real body just
;; landed with a no-op, a regression rather than the fix this idiom exists
;; for. jakx-logo-menu has no method-59 override anywhere and its own
;; deftype (menu2-h.gc:365) runs before base-menu's own stub
;; (menu2-installs.gc:593), so it is the one type still exposed.
(method-set! jakx-logo-menu 59 (method-of-type base-menu base-menu-method-59))

;; row-text family: real landing, issue 759, a2 rung's own STEP 4. Fresh
;; scoped redecode (same scratch recipe as slice 1; this worktree's own
;; out/jakx/fr3/GAME.fr3 verified byte-identical before and after), taken
;; AFTER this rung's own step 1 retyped string-menu.strings to
;; menu-string-array: that retype is what lets the decoder recognize
;; (-> this strings) as real sugar here at all, rather than the raw offset
;; chain slice 1's own base-menu-method-59 bodies still show for the same
;; field.
;;
;; Three classes of decompiler-only notation needed resolving here, none
;; covered by this file's own header (all confirmed by direct compilation):
;;   sll/+.s/*.si/<.si/>0.ui/<0.si are decompiler print names for raw shift
;;     and signed/unsigned ops it could not map back to plain GOAL syntax
;;     (decompiler/IR2/AtomicOp.cpp:289,311,329,848,890,894), not real GOAL
;;     forms (goalc/compiler/compilation/Atoms.cpp only knows "shl", never
;;     "sll"); rewritten to (shl ...)/(+ ...)/(* ...)/(< ...)/(> ... 0)/
;;     (< ... 0) at each site.
;;   f2i/fpr->gpr are likewise decompiler print names (AtomicOp.cpp:297 and
;;     unlisted; every other apparent usage anywhere in this tree, cam-
;;     debug.gc included, turns out to sit inside that file's own #| |#
;;     block comments and has never actually compiled), representing the
;;     MIPS o32 convention of converting a float to an int in a float
;;     register (f2i, i.e. cvt.w.s) then bit-copying that register into a
;;     general-purpose one to pass as a plain int argument (fpr->gpr, i.e.
;;     mfc1); GOAL's own register allocation makes the second step a no-op,
;;     so (f2i X) becomes (the int X) and (fpr->gpr X) becomes bare X.
;;   (dynamic-array-field-access BASE data PLACEHOLDER text), where BASE is
;;     (-> this strings) plus a raw 80*i offset: the decoder recognized
