;; a2 rung's own STEP 5. Donor menu2.gc:5031, 858 lines. Two branches on
;; whether this row's own info-ptr has a real box-index (-1 means none):
;;
;;   box-index == -1: the simple per-row draw. Calls string-menu-method-67
;;     to refresh text, then for each row builds a stack font-context from
;;     its own strings-info entry (position, width/height, scale, flags,
;;     color, alpha) and calls draw-string; closes the dma-buffer segment
;;     with a manual "next" tag (the same shape with-dma-bucket's own macro
;;     expansion writes, goal_src/jakx/engine/dma/dma-buffer.gc:281-306, but
;;     hand-inlined rather than macro-expanded because the donor guards the
;;     close behind "did anything actually get written" and that macro's
;;     own current body no longer does - a live divergence, not a
;;     transcription choice) and calls dma-bucket-insert-tag.
;;
;;   else: the auto-fit branch. Same string-menu-method-67 refresh, then
;;     per row: transforms the row's own strings-info position through
;;     joint-mat*offset-matrix (matrix*!/vector-matrix*!) into a scratch
;;     matrix that doubles as the row's own screen-space transform;
;;     optionally draws a red debug-line rectangle around the row's own
;;     text box (behind *draw-debug-boxes*, using that transform's own
;;     rvec/uvec/trans rows scaled by two raw per-menu extent fields); calls
;;     print-game-text once to measure the text's own rendered width (a2=#t,
;;     matching print-game-text's own "measure, don't draw" branch) against
;;     the row's own persisted scale; when get-player-amplitude (issue 759's
;;     own STEP 3 stub, always 0.0 here, so this specific fold never
;;     triggers at present) exceeds 5, blends a derived speed value into
;;     that scale first; then, while the scale stays above a small
;;     threshold and the measured width still exceeds the font-context's
;;     own height, repeatedly shrinks the scale by a fixed step and
;;     re-measures, before calling print-game-text for real (at whatever
